# Git identity

When committing or pushing, use Charlie’s identity and credentials — never Cursor’s bot/cloud author or Cursor-managed remotes.

- Prefer local git user / `gh` auth (GitHub: Charmander542).
- Do not set author/committer to Cursor Agent, cursor, or similar.
- Do not amend or rewrite commits to attribute them to Cursor.
- If push auth fails, ask Charlie to authenticate (`gh auth login` or SSH keys) instead of using a Cursor-owned remote or token.
- Never update git config unless explicitly asked.
